From david@UTEXAS  Fri May 16 06:21:30 1980
Date: 16 May 1980 at 0813-CDT
From: david at UTEXAS
Subject: Reply to: a new network news program
To: CSVAX.mark at Berkeley

I would certainly like to learn more about this news program.
Sounds like a very useful facility.

One suggestion I would have off-hand:  it would be desirable
to have a facility to have some person screen some categories
of news.  For instance, if there is a system news category, you
might want to allow only official system-types to mail to it.
For other categories some sites might want to screen messages
before they are retransmitted.
-------

From SWG@MIT-DMS  Fri May 16 06:35:45 1980
Date: 16 May 1980 0936-EDT
From: SWG at MIT-DMS (S. W. Galley)
To: CSVAX.mark at BERKELEY
In-reply-to: Message of 16 May 80 at 0400 EDT by CSVAX.mark@Berkeley
Subject: [Re: a new network news program]
Message-id: <[MIT-DMS].147206>

Our host might be interested in joining the news network.
We can't guarantee that the news would be handled exactly as you described,
since we don't run Unix, our support for C is chancy, and we have limited
resources for generating new programs.  However, it would be trivial to
forward all news to users requesting it, or to store it all in a file for
perusal.  We can't guarantee detection of multiple copies of the same news,
so we would have to be a leaf in the network.


